<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bogislaw IV, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1258–1309</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bogislaw IV, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a>. In 1295 he and his half-brother Otto I divided the Duchy of Pomerania: Bogislaw took the coastal lands north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peene">Peene</a> and the east, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolgast">Wolgast</a>, while Otto received the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Stettin</a>. The partition created the separate duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bogislaw-iv-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Bogislaw IV, Duke of Pomerania" width="112" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cornelius Krommeny · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bogislaw_IV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
